; HomerView.jkm -- HomerView's keys, for reference
;
; NOT WHAT BINDS THEM, AND THE REASON IS WORTH KNOWING. JAWS loads an
; application key map NAMED AFTER THE EXECUTABLE. Nothing on this machine is
; called HomerView.exe, so this file is never read by JAWS at all. What binds
; these keys is chainJawsScripts, which writes them into a key map named after
; the BROWSER -- msedge.jkm, chrome.jkm, or whatever ConfigNames.ini says that
; browser's settings are called.
;
; This copy is kept so the keys have one readable home in the project, and
; check 14 compares it against chainJawsScripts so the two cannot drift.
;
; SECTIONS MATTER MORE THAN KEYS HERE, and both of these sections now live
; inside the BROWSER'S own key map, so both are scoped to the browser.
;
; [Common Keys] applies in any cursor mode while the browser is in front: the
; address bar, a form field, focus mode. The commands that must answer from
; any of those are here.
;
; [Virtual Keys] applies only while the VIRTUAL CURSOR is active. Plain
; letters and single function keys belong here, because in a form field they
; would type themselves.
;
; NOTHING OF HOMERVIEW'S IS IN default.jkm ANY MORE. It used to be, and
; [Virtual Keys] there applies wherever a virtual cursor is active -- which
; includes an Outlook message, a Word document and a PDF. Control+O in Outlook
; was running HomerView's Open Document. Keys in the browser's own map do not
; exist anywhere else.
;
; Alt+JAWSKey+H is here and starts or returns to the browser while the browser
; is in front. Starting it from ANYWHERE ELSE is Alt+Control+H, a Windows
; shortcut key on the desktop icon, which is in no key map at all because it
; is not a screen reader command.

[Common Keys]
Alt+JAWSKey+A=hVCheckAccessibility
Alt+JAWSKey+C=hVFindContacts
Alt+JAWSKey+D=hVDismissDialog
Alt+JAWSKey+F10=hVShowHomerViewMenu
Alt+JAWSKey+H=hVLaunchHomerView
Alt+JAWSKey+I=hVCheckAccessibilityIbm
Alt+JAWSKey+L=hVCopyLogToClipboard
Alt+JAWSKey+Q=hVSayDiagnostics
Alt+Shift+B=hVChooseBrowser
Alt+Shift+H=hVHotKeyHelp
Alt+Shift+S=hVOpenSettings

[Virtual Keys]
Alt+Apostrophe=hVSayClipboard
Alt+C=hVCopyAppend
Alt+Control+F1=hVOpenSessionLog
Alt+F1=hVShowAbout
Alt+F3=hVFindWordAtCursor
Alt+F8=hVReadAll
Alt+L=hVDescribeLinkTarget
Alt+M=hVSayMetadata
Alt+N=hVListNames
Alt+R=hVRecentPages
Alt+Shift+Apostrophe=hVClearClipboard
Alt+Shift+F=hVOpenPageFolder
Alt+Shift+F1=hVOpenQuickStart
Alt+Shift+F3=hVFindWordAtCursorBackwards
Alt+Shift+F8=hVGoToSelectionStart
Alt+Shift+P=hVCopyPageLinks
Alt+Shift+W=hVDownloadFiles
Control+Apostrophe=hVSaveClipboard
Control+C=hVCopySelection
Control+F1=hVOpenUserGuide
Control+F11=hVElevateVersion
Control+F3=hVFindByPattern
Control+F8=hVCopyAll
Control+O=hVOpenDocument
Control+S=hVSavePage
Control+Shift+Apostrophe=hVAppendClipboard
Control+Shift+E=hVExtractByPattern
Control+Shift+F=hVFindBackwards
Control+Shift+F1=hVOpenDeveloperNotes
Control+Shift+F3=hVFindByPatternBackwards
Control+Shift+Y=hVYieldByPattern
F3=hVFindNext
F8=hVStartSelection
Shift+F1=hVShowHistory
Shift+F3=hVFindPrevious
Shift+F4=hVSayTabNames
Shift+F8=hVCompleteSelection
Shift+F9=hVExtractMainContent
Shift+Q=hVMoveToProbableMain
